# git-filter-repo --replace-message rules for scrub-git-history.sh
#
# Copy to scrub-replacements.local.txt (gitignored) and fill in YOUR real terms.
# One rule per line. `literal==>replacement` or `regex:PATTERN==>replacement`.
# This file's real version is never committed, so the sensitive strings you list
# here do not leak into the repo.
#
# Examples (replace with your actual leaked terms):
# Your Previous Employer Inc==>[previous employer]
# regex:\b3,?999\b==>[redacted]
# regex:\b549\b==>[redacted]
